original.raw_answer:
{"abstain":false,"answer":"The error occurs because `inject` is not imported. Add it to your existing `@angular/core` import:

```typescript
import { Injectable, inject } from '@angular/core';
```

Your functional guard can remain:

```typescript
export const guestGuard: CanActivateFn = (route, state) => {
  return inject(PermissionsService).canActivate();
};
```

According to page 1, `inject` comes from `@angular/core`, and functional guards can delegate to an injectable class using `inject(myGuard).canActivate()`.

This fixes the missing-name error. Your current service always returns `false`; it does not yet implement the user-check/dashboard-redirection logic. Page 1 lists `boolean`, `UrlTree`, and `RedirectCommand` as supported guard results, but does not provide that authentication implementation.","citations":["第1页"]}

